903
00:45:00.040 --> 00:45:00.420
Wow.
哇。

904
00:45:00.820 --> 00:45:01.540
You'll love it.
你会喜欢的。

905
00:45:01.600 --> 00:45:02.740
I do wear that all the time.
我确实经常说那句话。

906
00:45:02.740 --> 00:45:04.740
And then on the back it says, I'm fantastic.
然后背面写着，我太棒了。

907
00:45:05.900 --> 00:45:06.660
Same brain.
心有灵犀。

908
00:45:07.960 --> 00:45:13.180
We really liked this question because we both come from a long line of teachers.
我们非常喜欢这个问题，因为我们两家都有很长的教师渊源。

909
00:45:13.540 --> 00:45:16.180
Someone wanted to know if you remember a favorite teacher.
有人想知道你们是否还记得某个最喜欢的老师。

910
00:45:16.500 --> 00:45:21.180
There was one in particular, a guy named Mr. Blackman, my second grade teacher.
还真有一个特别的，一个叫布莱克曼先生的人，我二年级的老师。

911
00:45:22.480 --> 00:45:26.740
And he's the one who got me interested in acting in the first place.
就是他最初让我对表演产生了兴趣。

912
00:45:26.960 --> 00:45:30.920
We were doing like a pilgrims meet the Native Americans thing.
我们当时在排那种清教徒与美洲原住民相遇的戏。

913
00:45:31.140 --> 00:45:32.840
It was a long time ago.
那是很久以前的事了。

914
00:45:33.060 --> 00:45:36.000
So a lot was being glossed over for sure.
所以很多细节肯定都被一带而过了。

915
00:45:36.000 --> 00:45:41.880
But what I remember is we were rowing canoes and it was all mime.
但我记得的是我们在划独木舟，全都是哑剧表演。

916
00:45:42.000 --> 00:45:44.560
You know, we were sitting in little chairs in the classroom.
你知道的，我们就坐在教室里的小椅子上。

917
00:45:44.760 --> 00:45:45.580
It wasn't a big play.
那不是什么大话剧。

918
00:45:45.760 --> 00:45:47.160
It was just like an in-class thing.
就只是那种课堂里的小活动。

919
00:45:48.140 --> 00:45:51.080
And I started rowing the canoe, my mime rowing.
然后我开始划独木舟，我用哑剧动作划着。

920
00:45:51.220 --> 00:45:54.220
And then I changed my hands with the oar and rowed on the other side.
接着我换了下手里的桨，在另一边划。

921
00:45:54.520 --> 00:45:55.580
I'll never forget it.
我永远不会忘记。

922
00:45:55.660 --> 00:45:56.740
He singled me out.
他单独表扬了我。

923
00:45:56.900 --> 00:45:58.900
It's the first time I'd ever been singled out in any way.
那是我有生以来第一次受到这种关注。

924
00:46:00.080 --> 00:46:02.900
And he gave me a pat on the back and said,
他拍了拍我的背，说道，

925
00:46:03.440 --> 00:46:07.480
notice how Steve rowed on both sides of the canoe so he wouldn't go in a circle.
大家注意看史蒂夫是怎么在独木舟两边划桨的，这样就不会转圈了。

926
00:46:07.800 --> 00:46:12.940
And he kept the canoe straight, you know, in this mime, you know, miming the canoe.
而且他保持了独木舟直行，你知道的，在这个哑剧里，你知道的，模仿独木舟。

927
00:46:13.280 --> 00:46:15.920
And something about that really struck me.
有些东西真的触动了我。

928
00:46:16.060 --> 00:46:22.100
And I thought, and apart from that, he was just the most lovely guy and really kind to all the kids.
而且我想，抛开这些不谈，他真的是个极好的人，对所有孩子都非常慈祥。

929
00:46:22.220 --> 00:46:23.400
And everyone, it was fun.
每个人都觉得很开心。

930
00:46:23.560 --> 00:46:25.160
It was really just a fun class.
那真是一个欢乐的班级。

931
00:46:25.160 --> 00:46:27.220
And he did that for all the kids, too.
他对所有孩子都是这样的。

932
00:46:27.340 --> 00:46:34.080
He made them feel special about whatever talent they had, whether it was art or music or anything.
他让每个孩子都为自己拥有的才华感到特别，不管是美术、音乐还是别的什么。

933
00:46:34.480 --> 00:46:38.900
He really embraced, you know, everyone's abilities.
他真的包容了，你知道的，每个人的能力。

934
00:46:39.300 --> 00:46:44.220
You know, as little as they were in that moment as a second grader.
尽管当时大家作为二年级学生还那么小。

935
00:46:44.460 --> 00:46:45.320
But I'll never forget it.
但我永远不会忘记。

936
00:46:45.440 --> 00:46:47.240
Like being seen in that way.
那种被看见的感觉。

937
00:46:47.240 --> 00:46:47.900
Yeah, you're out-seen.
对，被彻底看见了。

938
00:46:48.180 --> 00:46:48.440
Yeah.
对。

939
00:46:48.580 --> 00:46:50.380
And it was, that was special.
而且，那感觉很特别。

940
00:46:50.480 --> 00:46:51.300
Something sort of clicked.
某种感觉突然开窍了。

941
00:46:51.480 --> 00:46:52.820
Like, oh, that felt good.
就觉得，哦，那种感觉真好。

942
00:46:53.460 --> 00:46:56.140
And so I guess I, I owe it all to him.
所以我想我，我这一切都归功于他。

943
00:46:56.660 --> 00:46:59.720
You know, Steve, I love that story because I have a similar story.
你知道吗，史蒂夫，我特别喜欢这个故事，因为我也有类似的经历。

944
00:46:59.900 --> 00:47:03.040
I took a summer school acting class and we had to do pantomime.
我上过一个暑期表演班，我们必须做哑剧。

945
00:47:03.420 --> 00:47:04.800
We had to mime things.
我们必须模仿各种事情。

946
00:47:04.960 --> 00:47:10.960
And my assignment was to go over to the refrigerator and get out some milk and pour it in a glass and drink it.
我的作业是走到冰箱前，拿点牛奶出来，倒进杯子里喝掉。

947
00:47:11.380 --> 00:47:12.580
And so I did it.
于是我照做了。

948
00:47:12.720 --> 00:47:18.540
And afterwards, the teacher said, did everyone notice how Jenna shut the refrigerator with her foot?
事后，老师说，大家注意到珍娜是用脚关冰箱的吗？

949
00:47:18.800 --> 00:47:19.160
Oh!
哦！

950
00:47:19.380 --> 00:47:20.560
Yeah, it's exactly it.
对，就是这样。

951
00:47:20.560 --> 00:47:24.340
And I was like, wait, I might be good at this because I didn't think.
然后我就想，等等，我可能挺擅长这个的，因为我刚才没多想。

952
00:47:24.920 --> 00:47:27.200
It just, I, maybe I have a little thing.
就是，我，也许我确实有点天赋。

953
00:47:27.380 --> 00:47:28.040
Right, exactly.
对，完全正确。

954
00:47:28.180 --> 00:47:32.080
You know, and then it just makes you feel like I might be good at this.
你知道的，然后这就会让你觉得，我或许真的很擅长这个。

955
00:47:32.260 --> 00:47:33.800
Or it might be something.
或者这可能会是个亮点。

956
00:47:34.100 --> 00:47:34.280
Yeah.
对。

957
00:47:34.400 --> 00:47:38.340
You know, it might be something that I'm actually, yeah, capable of.
你知道的，这可能是我真正能够胜任的事情。

958
00:47:38.540 --> 00:47:39.460
That's so fun.
那太有意思了。

959
00:47:39.460 --> 00:47:41.520
And it's not even like, look at me.
而且这甚至不是那种“快看我”的感觉。

960
00:47:41.740 --> 00:47:42.020
No.
不是。

961
00:47:42.820 --> 00:47:48.260
It's just a sense of, like one of the first senses of pride that you ever feel.
这只是一种感觉，就像你感受到的最早的自豪感之一。

962
00:47:48.420 --> 00:47:48.600
Yes.
没错。

963
00:47:48.720 --> 00:47:53.780
That you accomplish something completely on your own, not your parents and nothing that you were
你完全靠自己独立完成了一件事，不是靠父母，也不是按照别人的

964
00:47:53.780 --> 00:47:54.780
instructed to do.
指示去做。

965
00:47:54.880 --> 00:47:56.560
It's just something that you did naturally.
这只是你自然而然做成的事。

966
00:47:57.320 --> 00:48:01.160
And to have somebody notice it felt really good.
而且能有人注意到这一点，感觉真的很棒。

967
00:48:01.340 --> 00:48:03.480
And that's a great teacher in my mind.
在我看来，这真是一个伟大的老师。

968
00:48:03.700 --> 00:48:05.520
Somebody who can pick up on those things.
一个能够察觉到这些细节的人。

969
00:48:05.940 --> 00:48:06.120
Yeah.
对。

970
00:48:06.660 --> 00:48:08.380
Okay, I love this question.
好吧，我喜欢这个问题。

971
00:48:09.140 --> 00:48:09.920
Here it is.
题目是这样的。

972
00:48:10.060 --> 00:48:15.120
Are there any foods you don't eat anymore because of so many takes you had to do with
有没有什么食物，是因为拍摄时为了某个特定镜头

973
00:48:15.120 --> 00:48:16.180
that certain food?
吃得太多，以至于现在再也不吃了？

974
00:48:16.180 --> 00:48:18.380
It can be on the office or any other job.
不管是在办公室还是在其他工作里都算。

975
00:48:18.560 --> 00:48:19.840
I know mine right away.
我一下子就能想起来。

976
00:48:20.020 --> 00:48:22.060
It's that cake that we had to eat.
就是我们不得不吃的那款蛋糕。

977
00:48:22.180 --> 00:48:24.680
The ice cream cake for Meredith's birthday.
为了梅丽迪斯生日准备的冰淇淋蛋糕。

978
00:48:24.820 --> 00:48:25.860
Was it the Alliance?
是阿莱恩斯那次吗？

979
00:48:26.180 --> 00:48:30.700
We started filming at 730 in the morning and we were given a slice of cake.
我们早上七点半开始拍摄，然后发给我们了一块蛋糕。

980
00:48:30.860 --> 00:48:33.500
And, you know, this is a rookie move on my part.
而且，你知道，我当时真是个新人生疏。

981
00:48:33.500 --> 00:48:38.140
I took a plate with a big piece of cake and I took a huge bite in that first take.
我拿了一盘大块蛋糕，在第一个镜头里就咬了一大口。

982
00:48:38.400 --> 00:48:43.400
And by the end, my fork was shaking as it got close to my mouth because I was like, I can't,
结果到最后，当叉子靠近嘴边时我的手都在抖，因为我在想，我不能

983
00:48:43.400 --> 00:48:44.860
I can't eat it anymore.
我真的吃不下了。

984
00:48:45.440 --> 00:48:47.080
Anyway, I was asking you that.
总之，我本来是想问你们的。

985
00:48:47.280 --> 00:48:51.620
But clearly I have a visceral, like, I can't eat ice cream cake anymore.
但很明显我有了本能的排斥，比如，我再也不吃冰淇淋蛋糕了。

986
00:48:51.620 --> 00:48:52.640
That did it.
那次彻底把我整怕了。

987
00:48:52.820 --> 00:48:53.360
That did you in.
那次把你给坑惨了。

988
00:48:53.560 --> 00:48:54.280
Yeah, it's so gross to me.
对，现在想来觉得恶心透了。

989
00:48:54.440 --> 00:48:56.800
I learned early on to nibble.
我一开始就学会了要细嚼慢咽。

990
00:48:57.020 --> 00:48:57.420
Yeah.
对。

991
00:48:57.960 --> 00:49:03.880
Not like if that first take, try not to take a big bite because then you have to match it
就好像如果那是第一个镜头，尽量别咬太大口，因为接下来一整天

992
00:49:03.880 --> 00:49:05.440
for the rest of the day.
你都得保持和那个镜头一致。

993
00:49:05.680 --> 00:49:05.980
Yeah.
对。

994
00:49:07.440 --> 00:49:09.080
Or I'm not hungry today.
或者说我今天不饿。

995
00:49:09.400 --> 00:49:11.320
You know, my character's not hungry.
你知道的，我扮演的角色现在不饿。

996
00:49:12.300 --> 00:49:15.020
But Michael would eat some pretty crazy stuff.
不过迈克尔以前吃过一些挺疯狂的东西。

997
00:49:15.300 --> 00:49:20.920
I, nothing that turned my stomach, nothing to the point where I can't eat it anymore.
我倒没有什么让我倒胃口的，也没有到以后再也吃不下去的程度。

998
00:49:21.060 --> 00:49:27.300
I did a bit on The Daily Show where I was supposed to be eating Crisco.
我在《每日秀》里做过一个搞笑短片，当时要假装吃起酥油。

999
00:49:27.600 --> 00:49:29.780
I was doing, it was some health food segment.
我在做，那是一个关于健康食品的环节。

1000
00:49:30.020 --> 00:49:32.520
And I said, well, this is all vegetable based.
然后我说，好吧，这全都是植物成分的。

1001
00:49:32.780 --> 00:49:36.160
And I was like at the, at the desk with John.
然后我当时坐在桌子旁，和约翰在一起。

1002
00:49:36.160 --> 00:49:39.840
And so I, I take a big spoonful of Crisco.
然后我，我舀了一大勺克里斯科起酥油。

1003
00:49:40.080 --> 00:49:41.040
For real Crisco?
真的起酥油？

1004
00:49:41.280 --> 00:49:45.640
Well, they wanted to mock it up and just put like vanilla frosting in because no one would
嗯，他们本来想做个道具，直接放点香草糖霜进去，因为没人会

1005
00:49:45.640 --> 00:49:45.960
know.
知道。

1006
00:49:46.140 --> 00:49:47.580
And I could play it like it's Crisco.
而且我也可以把它当成起酥油来演。

1007
00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:53.080
But I said, no, leave Crisco in because that's going to be funnier for John to watch
但我说，不，别换，就用真的起酥油，因为看我吃起酥油对约翰来说会更有趣，因为他脸上的

1008
00:49:53.080 --> 00:49:59.460
me eat Crisco because the, the expression on his face was pretty horrifying and, and
表情相当吓人，而且

1009
00:49:59.460 --> 00:50:00.480
I didn't practice it.
我也没有提前排练过。

1010
00:50:00.580 --> 00:50:02.540
So I didn't know what I was getting myself into.
所以我根本不知道自己要面对的是什么。

1011
00:50:02.540 --> 00:50:08.440
And so on camera, basically live, you know, that show was live to tape, but it was really
所以在镜头前，基本上是现场直播——你知道，那个节目是录播，但效果真的

1012
00:50:08.440 --> 00:50:08.780
bad.
太糟了。

1013
00:50:09.080 --> 00:50:14.420
I did not, I could, I mean, the two of us had a hard time getting through the rest of that
我根本……我甚至，我是说，我们俩很难熬过那段节目的剩下部分，因为他

1014
00:50:14.420 --> 00:50:20.080
segment because he, he knew, he knew I was in distress.
他知道，他知道我很痛苦。

1015
00:50:22.220 --> 00:50:28.320
So, so not that I would sit around eating Crisco, but that, that kind of, that was a hard one.
所以，倒不是说我会没事坐着吃起酥油，但那次，那种感觉，那真是一个难关。

1016
00:50:28.480 --> 00:50:28.660
Yeah.
对。

1017
00:50:29.780 --> 00:50:30.840
Here's a good question.
这里有个好问题。

1018
00:50:30.840 --> 00:50:32.780
Do you have a Toby in your life?
你们的生活中也有个托比吗？

1019
00:50:33.200 --> 00:50:35.160
Someone who just enrages you.
那种会让你火冒三丈的人。

1020
00:50:35.420 --> 00:50:42.620
This was one of our favorite questions sent in because we're like, we're sure Steve doesn't
这是我们收到的最喜欢的提问之一，因为我们在想，我们确信史蒂夫

1021
00:50:42.620 --> 00:50:44.760
have a Toby, but, but yeah.
不会有个托比，但是，好吧。

1022
00:50:45.120 --> 00:50:47.360
Someone who just really for no reason.
就是那种莫名其妙的人。

1023
00:50:47.480 --> 00:50:48.360
You just hate.
你就是讨厌他。

1024
00:50:49.460 --> 00:50:51.140
Just abject hatred.
纯粹的厌恶。

1025
00:50:51.140 --> 00:50:59.660
Um, no, I don't, but that, that's, that's one of my favorite character dynamics of, of
嗯，不，我没有，但那，那是，那是我在《办公室》

1026
00:50:59.660 --> 00:51:02.000
the time that I spent on, on the office.
度过的时光中最喜欢的角色关系之一。

1027
00:51:02.200 --> 00:51:08.100
It, and it evolved from, I don't exactly, I know it's been discussed as to, and I think
它发展自——我不太清楚，我知道大家讨论过原因，而且我认为

1028
00:51:08.100 --> 00:51:15.580
the writers could sort of pinpoint clearly, but I think one day I just decided, I just,
编剧们也许能准确指出，但我觉得有一天我只是决定，我只是

1029
00:51:15.580 --> 00:51:22.340
I just, I just got really mad at him and like disgusted by him for no reason.
我只是，毫无理由地突然对火冒三丈，并且对他感到厌恶。

1030
00:51:22.580 --> 00:51:25.200
And we just kind of stayed with it.
然后我们就顺着这种设定演下去了。

1031
00:51:25.340 --> 00:51:26.700
People lost it.
大家都笑疯了。

1032
00:51:26.980 --> 00:51:31.200
They would lose it at a table read when you would snap at Toby.
每次你在剧本围读时对托比发飙，他们都会笑得前仰后合。

1033
00:51:31.480 --> 00:51:34.600
We did an interview with Paul and he said he remembers the moment.
我们采访过保罗，他说他记得那个时刻。

1034
00:51:34.760 --> 00:51:35.240
Oh, he does?
哦，他记得？

1035
00:51:35.480 --> 00:51:40.220
It was during the Alliance when he has to come in the office and sign Meredith's birthday
那是拍摄《同盟》那一集时，他走进办公室要在梅雷迪思的生日

1036
00:51:40.220 --> 00:51:48.720
card and apparently it just took him a long time to write and you turned on him and you
卡片上签字，显然他写了很长时间，然后你突然转向他

1037
00:51:48.720 --> 00:51:53.260
told him, you said, I don't know what it is, Paul, but I hate you for how long it's taken
对他说，我不知道为什么，保罗，但我恨死你写这张卡片花了这么长时间了

1038
00:51:53.260 --> 00:52:00.430
you to write this card and you guys laughed so hard about it.
然后你们俩为此笑得不行。

1039
00:52:00.810 --> 00:52:06.370
And you met like me as Michael, like Michael is so irritated with you right now.
当时你是作为迈克尔的立场——就像迈克尔现在对你烦透了。

1040
00:52:06.570 --> 00:52:10.970
And that, that was like, everyone else just signed their name, but he started to write
而且，那就像，其他人都在上面签了自己的名字，但他却开始写

1041
00:52:10.970 --> 00:52:11.450
something.
点别的什么。

1042
00:52:11.750 --> 00:52:11.810
Yeah.
对。

1043
00:52:12.070 --> 00:52:17.730
I, it was, I love the fact that it was never discussed too, as to why, um, and the specifics
我，我很喜欢的一点是，关于为什么以及其中的具体细节

1044
00:52:17.730 --> 00:52:18.150
of it.
从未被讨论过。

1045
00:52:18.250 --> 00:52:18.510
Yeah.
对。

1046
00:52:18.790 --> 00:52:20.610
And, and people have asked me that too.
而且人们也问过我这个问题。

1047
00:52:20.710 --> 00:52:22.770
Well, why, why does Michael hate Toby so much?
“唉，为什么，为什么迈克尔那么讨厌托比？”

1048
00:52:22.870 --> 00:52:27.670
And I think it, well, I think it's like the end when our characters say goodbye to each
而我觉得，嗯，我觉得就像最后当我们的角色互相告别时

1049
00:52:27.670 --> 00:52:34.670
other, I, that's, I'll never talk about exactly what was said because that's, that's like
那样，我永远不会透露当时具体说了什么，因为那是

1050
00:52:34.670 --> 00:52:35.030
our thing.
我们之间的秘密。

1051
00:52:35.170 --> 00:52:39.810
And I, and it's more fun to, to leave those things as sort of a mystery.
而且我觉得，把这些事情当成某种谜团其实更有趣。

1052
00:52:39.810 --> 00:52:41.090
Like, well, why really?
比如，究竟是为什么呢？

1053
00:52:41.450 --> 00:52:47.250
Cause I, I built in Michael's head, like all of the reasons, but it's better that you
因为我在迈克尔的脑海里构建了所有的理由，但你最好还是

1054
00:52:47.250 --> 00:52:47.750
don't know.
不知道。

1055
00:52:47.910 --> 00:52:48.170
Yeah.
对。

1056
00:52:48.270 --> 00:52:49.490
That it's just kind of sits there.
就让它那样留白。

1057
00:52:49.910 --> 00:52:51.930
That's how I feel about the teapot letter.
我对那个茶壶信也是这种感觉。

1058
00:52:52.070 --> 00:52:52.290
Right.
没错。

1059
00:52:52.590 --> 00:52:54.550
Everyone wants to know what's in the teapot letter.
大家都想知道茶壶信里写了什么。

1060
00:52:54.810 --> 00:52:59.950
And the thing is, is that what's in the teapot letter is what you need to be in the teapot
问题在于，茶壶信里该写的内容，就是那些需要出现在茶壶

1061
00:52:59.950 --> 00:53:00.190
letter.
信里的内容。

1062
00:53:00.490 --> 00:53:02.750
There's what I needed to be in the teapot letter.
那是我认为茶壶信里需要有的东西。

1063
00:53:02.750 --> 00:53:09.310
There's the thing that Pam needs, but like, it has to be the most wonderful romantic thing
那是潘需要的东西，但它必须是最浪漫美妙的事物

1064
00:53:09.310 --> 00:53:11.010
and you can't write it.
而你根本写不出来。

1065
00:53:11.130 --> 00:53:13.170
Like you can't tell people what was in it.
就像你不能告诉大家里面到底写了什么一样。

1066
00:53:13.410 --> 00:53:14.690
It'll just be a letdown.
那只会让人失望。

1067
00:53:14.950 --> 00:53:15.370
It will.
确实会的。

1068
00:53:15.510 --> 00:53:16.790
It can't live up to it.
它承受不起这样的期待。

1069
00:53:16.870 --> 00:53:17.010
Right.
没错。

1070
00:53:17.170 --> 00:53:18.830
So it's like, I know what it said.
所以这就好比，我知道上面写了什么。

1071
00:53:19.110 --> 00:53:19.510
Completely.
完全清楚。

1072
00:53:19.670 --> 00:53:22.910
But it's better if, if you write it yourself as an audience member.
但作为观众，你自己来脑补会更好。

1073
00:53:23.110 --> 00:53:26.470
I, I think the writers in general felt that way about the show.
我、我觉得编剧们对这部剧的总体看法也是这样的。

1074
00:53:26.470 --> 00:53:31.410
And I think Greg was very savvy about that, that you don't have to tell the whole story
而且我觉得格雷格在这方面非常有远见，你不需要把整个故事全盘托出

1075
00:53:31.410 --> 00:53:33.770
and just let people come to it.
只要让观众自己去体会就行。

1076
00:53:33.830 --> 00:53:38.110
And I think that's partly why people have liked the show over the years is it doesn't
我想这也是为什么多年来大家一直喜欢这部剧的部分原因，因为它并没有

1077
00:53:38.110 --> 00:53:42.050
spell everything out about these characters or about these relationships.
把这些角色或这些关系的方方面面都直白地解释清楚。

1078
00:53:42.130 --> 00:53:47.710
You kind of acquire a knowledge over time and it becomes more ingrained that way.
随着时间的推移，你自然会有一种了解，这种了解会变得更加根深蒂固。

1079
00:53:47.890 --> 00:53:52.510
This is sort of off the subject, but you know, you talking about the teapot letter
这有点偏离主题了，不过你知道的，你刚才谈到茶壶信

1080
00:53:52.510 --> 00:53:58.050
and, you know, and I've thought about this many, many times since I left the show that
而且，你知道的，自从我离开剧组后，我曾多次想过这件事，那就是

1081
00:53:58.050 --> 00:54:04.390
you and John, in my opinion, you and John were the, the rock of that show.
在我的看法里，你和约翰，你和约翰是那部剧的基石。

1082
00:54:04.550 --> 00:54:11.490
Like if not for your two characters, I feel like that show would have imploded because there
如果不是你们两个角色，我觉得那部剧就会分崩离析，因为当时

1083
00:54:11.490 --> 00:54:17.230
was, there was so much craziness going on and so much wackiness and you were both such
有太多疯狂和古怪的事情在上演，而你们两个在剧中扮演了如此

1084
00:54:17.230 --> 00:54:26.210
grounded characters on that show while simultaneously being incredibly funny and real, but the fact
脚踏实地的角色，同时又极其搞笑和真实，最重要的是

1085
00:54:26.210 --> 00:54:35.170
that everyone could bounce off of you and your very grounded, loving and interesting relationship
每个人都能在你们以及你们那种脚踏实地、充满爱意且有趣的感情上找到共鸣

1086
00:54:35.170 --> 00:54:39.590
and how that grew to me, that was the nucleus of the show.
看着这种关系如何成长，对我和整个剧来说，那就是核心所在。

1087
00:54:39.750 --> 00:54:41.130
I I've always felt that way.
我一直都是这么觉得的。

1088
00:54:41.130 --> 00:54:45.470
And the way that you guys, and you're both such good actors too.
而且你们俩，而且你们俩也都是极好的演员。

1089
00:54:45.890 --> 00:54:51.350
It's like, we were just so fortunate on so many fronts in terms of the casting of this
这就好比，我们在很多方面都太幸运了，无论是这部剧的

1090
00:54:51.350 --> 00:54:56.730
show, in terms of the writing, I attribute it to, well, to you guys, obviously, and to
演员阵容，还是剧本创作，我都要归功于，嗯，当然是归功于你们，还有

1091
00:54:56.730 --> 00:55:03.030
Greg for like putting this group of people together in just the right sort of alchemy.
格雷格，因为他通过某种恰到好处的化学反应把这群人聚在了一起。

1092
00:55:03.290 --> 00:55:08.410
I don't know if I've ever specifically told you that, but I've, I've always felt that way.
我不知道我是否曾对你明确说过这些，但我一直、一直都是这么想的。

1093
00:55:08.990 --> 00:55:10.510
Steve, thank you.
史蒂夫，谢谢你。

1094
00:55:11.310 --> 00:55:17.630
I remember when we got ready to shoot the pilot, Steven and Ricky came to visit and we had
我记得我们准备拍摄试播集时，史蒂文和瑞奇来探班，我们和他们

1095
00:55:17.630 --> 00:55:23.750
like this one day meeting with them and Steven told John and I never forget you two are the
开了一整天的会，史蒂文对约翰和我——我永远不会忘记——说你们俩是

1096
00:55:23.750 --> 00:55:24.390
heart of the show.
节目的核心。

1097
00:55:24.910 --> 00:55:29.970
And I remember it was like in Threat Level Midnight, I was like, gulp, gulp.
我记得当时就像在拍《威胁级午夜》时一样，我忍不住咽了咽口水。

1098
00:55:30.650 --> 00:55:33.730
I thought, I don't really know what that means.
心想，我其实不太明白那是什么意思。

1099
00:55:33.850 --> 00:55:35.270
I, that's sort of scary to me.
我觉得这对我来说有点吓人。

1100
00:55:35.270 --> 00:55:42.230
I was sort of hoping to kind of keep with my whole like wallflower thing where Pam just
我本来还希望保持我那种透明人的风格，也就是让潘只是

1101
00:55:42.230 --> 00:55:46.870
kind of sits at the desk and gives a couple of stares, really liking that lane.
就坐在办公桌旁，眼神里充满挑衅，真的很喜欢那种状态。

1102
00:55:47.290 --> 00:55:49.890
But over time, I understood what he meant.
但随着时间推移，我明白了他说的话是什么意思。

1103
00:55:49.990 --> 00:55:53.910
And it's, it's kind of what you're saying, which is like, we're not going to go to you
而且这，这有点像你刚才说的，也就是，我们不会总来找你

1104
00:55:53.910 --> 00:56:01.710
all the time or maybe even very often, but over a large arc, over a large period of time,
或者甚至不会经常来，但从长远来看，在漫长的时间跨度里，

1105
00:56:01.870 --> 00:56:03.450
this is a really important thing.
这是一件非常重要的事情。

1106
00:56:03.770 --> 00:56:07.490
And so just, you know, make sure you always honor it.
所以，你知道的，确保你始终重视它。

1107
00:56:07.730 --> 00:56:10.950
Make sure that you, you know, that you honor that.
确保你，你知道的，确保你重视这一点。

1108
00:56:10.950 --> 00:56:11.290
We did.
我们做到了。

1109
00:56:11.450 --> 00:56:18.130
I'm so glad Jim and Pam made it and work and they didn't like do that thing where they
我很高兴吉姆和潘最终走到了一起并且感情稳定，他们没有那种

1110
00:56:18.790 --> 00:56:20.230
pull you apart and put you back together.
先拆散你们再让你们复合的烂俗套路。

1111
00:56:20.470 --> 00:56:21.550
The breakup, makeup, makeup, makeup.
分分合合，合合合合。

1112
00:56:21.890 --> 00:56:22.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1113
00:56:22.290 --> 00:56:26.170
And I get really defensive, Jim and Pam, if like we're doing an interview and someone's
而且我护短得很，针对吉姆和潘，要是有人在采访时

1114
00:56:26.170 --> 00:56:29.170
like to Jenna, I think Jim and Pam are still together.
对珍娜说，我觉得吉姆和潘现在还在一块吗？

1115
00:56:29.350 --> 00:56:30.690
I'm like, how dare you?
我就会想，你怎么敢这么说？

1116
00:56:31.250 --> 00:56:32.890
Of course they're still together.
他们当然还在一起。

1117
00:56:33.030 --> 00:56:35.670
And so are Dwight and Angela and so are Michael and Holly.
德怀特和安吉拉也是，迈克尔和霍莉也是。

1118
00:56:36.550 --> 00:56:37.130
Get out of here.
一边去吧。

1119
00:56:37.210 --> 00:56:37.890
Oh, you know what?
哦，你知道吗？

1120
00:56:37.910 --> 00:56:38.650
I need to tell you about.
我得跟你讲讲。

1121
00:56:38.810 --> 00:56:39.210
No.
不要。

1122
00:56:39.430 --> 00:56:40.070
Oh, dear.
噢，天哪。

1123
00:56:40.070 --> 00:56:40.730
No.
不要。

1124
00:56:41.010 --> 00:56:41.710
About Michael and Holly.
关于迈克尔和霍莉的。

1125
00:56:41.850 --> 00:56:42.090
No.
不要。

1126
00:56:44.410 --> 00:56:44.870
No.
不要。

1127
00:56:45.110 --> 00:56:46.690
Oh, it is bad.
哦，这可真够糟糕的。

1128
00:56:46.690 --> 00:56:47.510
It is bad.
真挺糟糕的。

1129
00:56:47.770 --> 00:56:50.190
Oh, I don't want to, I don't want to get into it.
哦，我不想，我不想深入聊这个。

1130
00:56:50.530 --> 00:56:56.650
We just watched the scene and it's, you know, I feel like I'm rediscovering so many of these
我们刚看了那场戏，而且，你知道的，我觉得我正在重新发现其中的许多戏份

1131
00:56:56.650 --> 00:57:00.350
scenes because we haven't seen the show since it aired, you know, a lot of these episodes.
因为自从剧集播出以来，很多这样的剧集我们都没再看过了，你知道的。

1132
00:57:00.590 --> 00:57:06.710
But when you and Amy Ryan do that, you are, hoo-ha, like that moment.
但当你和艾米·莱恩那样演的时候，你们俩，哇哦，就那种时刻。

1133
00:57:06.710 --> 00:57:08.930
And it says basically, I love you.
那句话基本上就是在说，我爱你。

1134
00:57:08.930 --> 00:57:10.070
You're like, yo, wicked smart.
就像是在说，嘿，聪明绝顶。

1135
00:57:10.250 --> 00:57:10.510
You are.
你就是这样。

1136
00:57:10.610 --> 00:57:12.490
It's like, I was like tearing up.
当时我简直快感动哭了。

1137
00:57:12.730 --> 00:57:12.990
Yeah.
是啊。

1138
00:57:13.170 --> 00:57:14.230
I like played it for Jenna.
我还放给珍娜看了。

1139
00:57:14.370 --> 00:57:15.710
I was like, you got to watch the scene.
我当时说，你得看看这场戏。

1140
00:57:15.890 --> 00:57:18.510
They're just saying you are, but it's like so powerful.
他们虽然只是在说你很棒，但那种感觉太震撼了。

1141
00:57:19.110 --> 00:57:19.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1142
00:57:19.550 --> 00:57:20.450
Amy Ryan's pretty good.
艾米·莱恩演得挺好的。

1143
00:57:20.650 --> 00:57:20.850
Yeah.
是啊。

1144
00:57:20.970 --> 00:57:21.250
She's okay.
她还行吧。

1145
00:57:21.250 --> 00:57:22.130
She was fine.
她表现得不错。

1146
00:57:22.370 --> 00:57:26.570
I mean, I guess we were lucky to get her in the show.
我是说，能请她来演这部剧，我们可真是走运。

1147
00:57:27.630 --> 00:57:30.010
She did pretty well for herself, I think.
我觉得她现在的成就也算实至名归了。

1148
00:57:30.730 --> 00:57:31.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1149
00:57:31.150 --> 00:57:33.090
We did just watch all of these episodes.
我们确实刚刚看完了所有这些剧集。

1150
00:57:33.420 --> 00:57:38.270
We watched the proposal to Holly and the singing goodbye to you.
我们看了向霍莉求婚的那段，还有深情告别的那段。

1151
00:57:38.390 --> 00:57:38.570
Yeah.
对。

1152
00:57:38.570 --> 00:57:43.390
And, you know, all the individual goodbyes to all the different people.
而且，你懂的，要向所有不同的人一一告别。

1153
00:57:44.130 --> 00:57:46.970
What a brutal couple of final weeks for you.
对你来说，最后这几周可真够残酷的。

1154
00:57:47.450 --> 00:57:51.350
I mean, were we, did we just cry the whole time?
我是说，我们当时是不是一直在哭？

1155
00:57:51.530 --> 00:57:52.290
How did we do that?
我们是怎么熬过来的？

1156
00:57:53.030 --> 00:57:53.810
I don't know.
我不知道。

1157
00:57:53.810 --> 00:57:57.670
I, you know, I could look at it that I'm, I'm, yeah, I don't know.
我，你知道，我可以换个角度看，我，我，对，我不知道。

1158
00:57:57.830 --> 00:58:03.430
I don't want to make too much of it, but it, it was, it was difficult because, you know,
我不想小题大做，但它确实，确实挺不容易的，因为，你知道的，

1159
00:58:03.530 --> 00:58:10.490
we were such good friends and it, it had been so much fun and so rewarding in a lot of ways,
我们曾是那么好的朋友，而且，在很多方面，这都充满乐趣、收获颇丰，

1160
00:58:10.630 --> 00:58:11.210
all ways.
方方面面。

1161
00:58:11.570 --> 00:58:16.050
But at the same time, there was this, for me, there was a joy to it.
但与此同时，对我来说，其中也有一种喜悦。

1162
00:58:16.250 --> 00:58:20.870
You know, when you, you're crying with joy because it wasn't even sadness.
你知道，当你因为喜极而泣时，那甚至都不是悲伤。

1163
00:58:20.970 --> 00:58:22.150
Like, cause I was ready.
就像，因为我已经准备好了。

1164
00:58:22.290 --> 00:58:23.010
I was ready to go.
我已经准备好离开了。

1165
00:58:23.930 --> 00:58:27.110
And so I wasn't sad about leaving.
所以我并不是为离开而难过。

1166
00:58:27.570 --> 00:58:27.710
Yeah.
对。

1167
00:58:27.930 --> 00:58:29.370
And it felt right for Michael.
而且这很符合迈克尔的状态。

1168
00:58:29.630 --> 00:58:29.910
Yeah.
对。

1169
00:58:29.970 --> 00:58:31.430
No, it was, it was time.
没错，就是，是时候了。

1170
00:58:31.610 --> 00:58:36.310
And it was time, it was time for other characters to kind of step to the forefront and, and other
而且是时候了，是时候让其他角色走到聚光灯下，并且去推进

1171
00:58:36.310 --> 00:58:37.850
storylines to be pursued.
其他的故事线了。

1172
00:58:37.970 --> 00:58:41.890
It was just, I think it was the right, it was the timing was right.
这只是，我觉得很合适，时机刚刚好。

1173
00:58:42.050 --> 00:58:48.610
I think for everybody, but simultaneously, there was just a sense of joy for me that we had
我觉得对每个人来说都是如此，但与此同时，我内心也有一种喜悦感，因为我们

1174
00:58:48.610 --> 00:58:52.930
experienced all of this and we were getting, I was getting a chance.
经历这一切，而我们正在获得，我也正在获得一个机会。

1175
00:58:52.930 --> 00:58:58.190
To kind of take a lap with everybody and the way, you know, those last few episodes were
能和所有人一起，以那种方式，就是最后那几集安排的

1176
00:58:58.190 --> 00:58:58.570
structured.
结构那样，去绕场一周。

1177
00:58:58.870 --> 00:59:05.990
It felt very rich to me to kind of simultaneously be saying goodbye as Michael and, you know,
这让我感到非常充实，既是在以迈克尔的身份说再见，你知道的，

1178
00:59:06.090 --> 00:59:11.050
us as, as friends, you know, in this moment of work together.
也是我们作为朋友，你知道的，在这段共同工作的时光里告别。

1179
00:59:11.310 --> 00:59:13.070
But yeah, it was a lot.
不过确实，感触很多。

1180
00:59:13.210 --> 00:59:15.110
It was a very emotional thing.
这是一件非常情绪化的事。

1181
00:59:15.110 --> 00:59:19.070
It was like, it was, it was just hitting us in waves.
就像是，那种感觉，一阵接一阵地涌上心头。

1182
00:59:19.070 --> 00:59:23.110
I remember like we would laugh one minute and then we'd be tearing up the next.
我记得我们前一秒还在笑，下一秒就眼泪汪汪了。

1183
00:59:23.430 --> 00:59:26.370
But like you said, it's because we had had such a great run.
但就像你说的，那是因为我们曾有过一段那么棒的经历。

1184
00:59:26.650 --> 00:59:27.950
We'd had such a good time.
我们度过了那么美好的时光。

1185
00:59:28.310 --> 00:59:28.510
Incredible.
难以置信。

1186
00:59:28.970 --> 00:59:29.550
Just incredible.
简直难以置信。

1187
00:59:30.310 --> 00:59:34.430
Steve, we are always telling people when they ask us, what was it like to work with Steve
史蒂夫，每当别人问我们“和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔一起工作是什么体验”时，我们总是告诉他们，

1188
00:59:34.430 --> 00:59:34.770
Carell?
