1366
01:05:18.910 --> 01:05:20.270
We made them for everybody.
我们给每个人都调了一杯。

1367
01:05:20.270 --> 01:05:23.750
And we were like, damn, it's actually pretty good.
然后我们觉得，天哪，其实还挺好喝的。

1368
01:05:23.750 --> 01:05:29.930
I want to order one at a bar, but I'm, I'm scared to because, well, you have to come
我想在酒吧点一杯，但我又有点害怕，因为，嗯，你得

1369
01:05:29.930 --> 01:05:32.870
up with a name for it instead of Scotch and Splenda.
给它起个名字，而不能直接叫苏格兰威士忌加代糖。

1370
01:05:33.030 --> 01:05:34.110
Do you call it a Scotch-da?
你管它叫苏格兰代糖威士忌吗？

1371
01:05:34.730 --> 01:05:35.290
I know.
我知道。

1372
01:05:35.470 --> 01:05:39.370
Didn't, didn't Michael have a name for it and we can't remember what it is.
迈克不是给它起过名字吗，只是我们记不起来是什么了。

1373
01:05:39.870 --> 01:05:40.630
I don't know.
我不知道。

1374
01:05:41.310 --> 01:05:41.510
A splotch.
Splotch。

1375
01:05:41.510 --> 01:05:43.330
Yeah, he does have a name for it.
对，他确实给它起了个名字。

1376
01:05:43.470 --> 01:05:43.750
A splotch.
Splotch。

1377
01:05:43.970 --> 01:05:45.490
Wasn't it a Splenda and Scotch?
不叫代糖威士忌吗？

1378
01:05:45.610 --> 01:05:46.510
A splotch.
Splotch。

1379
01:05:46.630 --> 01:05:47.210
A splotch?
Splotch？

1380
01:05:47.370 --> 01:05:48.070
Maybe a splotch.
可能是 Splotch 吧。

1381
01:05:48.110 --> 01:05:48.590
Oh, that's good.
哦，这个名字不错。

1382
01:05:48.590 --> 01:05:49.710
It doesn't sound delicious.
听起来可不太美味。

1383
01:05:49.710 --> 01:05:50.510
It's very good.
非常好喝。

1384
01:05:50.650 --> 01:05:50.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1385
01:05:50.830 --> 01:05:52.430
I'll take a splotch, please.
请给我来一杯 Splotch。

1386
01:05:52.650 --> 01:05:53.190
You know what?
你知道吗？

1387
01:05:53.210 --> 01:05:54.490
I'll try a splotch at some point.
我什么时候一定要尝尝 Splotch。

1388
01:05:54.670 --> 01:05:54.890
Great.
太好了。

1389
01:05:55.370 --> 01:05:55.630
All right.
行吧。

1390
01:05:55.710 --> 01:05:55.830
Okay.
好的。

1391
01:05:56.010 --> 01:05:56.410
Next time.
下次吧。

1392
01:05:56.630 --> 01:05:57.670
The three of us are going to get together.
我们三个要聚一聚。

1393
01:05:57.890 --> 01:05:59.290
And we're going to have one splotch.
然后我们要喝上一杯 Splotch。

1394
01:05:59.470 --> 01:06:00.370
We're going to go splotching.
我们要去喝 Splotch 啦。

1395
01:06:01.750 --> 01:06:02.550
Last question.
最后一个问题。

1396
01:06:02.810 --> 01:06:06.150
When was the last time you had to get out your toolbox and what tool did you grab?
你上一次不得不拿出工具箱是什么时候？你拿了什么工具？

1397
01:06:06.450 --> 01:06:07.530
About three days ago.
大约三天前。

1398
01:06:07.670 --> 01:06:07.930
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1399
01:06:08.590 --> 01:06:14.720
I was putting, I am, I, I am so embarrassed.
我当时在装，我是说，我，我，我太尴尬了。

1400
01:06:15.040 --> 01:06:16.840
Are you about to say you're putting together a bird feeder?
你该不会要说你在组装鸟屋吧？

1401
01:06:17.560 --> 01:06:17.960
Worse.
更糟。

1402
01:06:19.160 --> 01:06:21.260
I bought, I bought.
我买了，我买了。

1403
01:06:22.240 --> 01:06:29.020
I bought a vacuum, an outdoor leaf vacuum, which also mulches the leaves.
我买了一个吸尘器，一个户外的树叶吸尘器，它还能把树叶粉碎。

1404
01:06:29.680 --> 01:06:33.260
And I had to go to my toolbox to put it together.
而且我得去工具箱拿工具把它组装起来。

1405
01:06:33.520 --> 01:06:34.440
I, I ordered it.
我，我订购了它。

1406
01:06:34.580 --> 01:06:34.840
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1407
01:06:34.980 --> 01:06:37.460
And it arrived and I had to assemble it.
然后它送到了，我必须自己组装。

1408
01:06:37.640 --> 01:06:37.840
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1409
01:06:37.920 --> 01:06:39.460
And put the little bag on it.
还要把那个小袋子装上。

1410
01:06:40.580 --> 01:06:42.060
Do you blow leaves?
你会吹树叶吗？

1411
01:06:42.240 --> 01:06:43.620
Well, I have a leaf blower too.
嗯，我也有一个吹叶机。

1412
01:06:43.780 --> 01:06:49.520
What I do, what I do is I, I use the leaf blower to blow them into a pile.
我是怎么做的呢，我用吹叶机把它们吹成一堆。

1413
01:06:49.520 --> 01:06:55.500
And then I take my vacuum mulcher and I, I, I vacuum them up and mulch the leaves.
然后我拿着我的吸叶粉碎机，我，我把它们吸起来并粉碎树叶。

1414
01:06:55.520 --> 01:06:58.740
And then I take the leaves and I put them in our planting beds.
接着我把这些树叶放进我们的花坛里。

1415
01:06:59.140 --> 01:06:59.980
Oh my God.
天哪。

1416
01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:03.120
And so that's, so the fife.
所以这就是，所以是横笛。

1417
01:07:04.060 --> 01:07:04.700
Pittsburgh.
匹兹堡。

1418
01:07:05.380 --> 01:07:08.580
Pizza, plain chocolate ice cream.
比萨饼，纯巧克力冰淇淋。

1419
01:07:11.520 --> 01:07:12.960
And that's, that's me.
这就是，这就是我。

1420
01:07:12.960 --> 01:07:13.200
Yeah.
是啊。

1421
01:07:13.400 --> 01:07:15.060
And we all do it in Pittsburgh.
我们在匹兹堡都是这样的。

1422
01:07:15.260 --> 01:07:15.560
Ew.
呃。

1423
01:07:17.300 --> 01:07:18.320
Barrel of laughs.
真是一场笑话。

1424
01:07:18.560 --> 01:07:21.020
Oh, I'm in love with you.
哦，我爱上你了。

1425
01:07:25.120 --> 01:07:33.060
Well, clearly the bar is low because there's, there's, there's not, I can't even believe that
好吧，显然标准很低，因为根本没有，我甚至不敢相信

1426
01:07:33.060 --> 01:07:36.880
Nancy decided to marry me with like that as a track record.
南希竟然敢嫁给我，带着这种过往记录。

1427
01:07:36.880 --> 01:07:39.660
That is the, that is, that's pretty bad.
这真的是，这真的是，相当糟糕。

1428
01:07:40.060 --> 01:07:45.220
Like when you do interviews like this and you say things and you hear yourself reflected
就像当你做这样的采访，说出这些话，然后听到自己

1429
01:07:45.220 --> 01:07:48.420
in the words, how you're describing yourself.
说出的那些词句，你对自己的描述。

1430
01:07:48.740 --> 01:07:54.280
I think I'm like more interesting than that, but clearly I'm not.
我觉得我应该比这更有趣，但显然我并没有。

1431
01:07:54.440 --> 01:07:55.860
I don't know how to play the piano.
我不会弹钢琴。

1432
01:07:56.260 --> 01:07:56.780
No.
不。

1433
01:07:56.900 --> 01:07:58.160
I, what would you like to do?
我，你想做什么？

1434
01:07:58.320 --> 01:08:03.180
I'd like to be smart and play the piano, but instead I'm mulching leaves and playing the
我想变得聪明并弹钢琴，但相反我却在粉碎树叶和吹

1435
01:08:03.180 --> 01:08:03.500
fife.
横笛。

1436
01:08:04.080 --> 01:08:04.240
So.
所以。

1437
01:08:05.840 --> 01:08:06.280
Okay.
好吧。

1438
01:08:06.720 --> 01:08:11.100
Is there anything in your career that you haven't done that you'd like to do or in your
在你的职业生涯中，有什么你还没做过但你想做的，或者在你的

1439
01:08:11.100 --> 01:08:11.400
life?
生活中？

1440
01:08:11.580 --> 01:08:12.740
Because like Jenna, for example.
因为就像珍娜，比如说。

1441
01:08:13.220 --> 01:08:13.620
Yes.
是的。

1442
01:08:13.780 --> 01:08:18.400
You know, it is my dream to one day do theater and win a Tony award.
你知道，我的梦想是有一天能演话剧并赢得托尼奖。

1443
01:08:18.600 --> 01:08:18.800
Yes.
是的。

1444
01:08:18.840 --> 01:08:20.840
This is my, I would love to do this in my life.
这是我的，我很想在我的生活中实现这一点。

1445
01:08:21.020 --> 01:08:26.240
My dream is I really want one of those hats that has big flowers on it that hummingbirds
我的梦想是我真的很想要那种上面有大花的帽子，有蜂鸟

1446
01:08:26.240 --> 01:08:26.980
eat out of.
会从上面采蜜。

1447
01:08:28.120 --> 01:08:31.060
So that's, Jenna wants to work towards a Tony.
所以这就是，珍娜想为托尼奖而努力。

1448
01:08:31.060 --> 01:08:34.440
I want to work towards a hummingbird eating out of my hat.
我想为让蜂鸟在我的帽子上采蜜而努力。

1449
01:08:35.260 --> 01:08:36.280
Where do you land?
你呢？

1450
01:08:36.300 --> 01:08:38.460
Those are very disparate dreaMs.
这些是截然不同的梦想。

1451
01:08:43.950 --> 01:08:46.810
Well, I don't even know how to top that.
好吧，我都不知道该怎么接话了。

1452
01:08:47.970 --> 01:08:55.650
Honestly, boy, I, I'm so content with certainly my professional life.
说实话，孩子，我，我对自己的职业生涯真的很满足。

1453
01:08:55.650 --> 01:08:57.150
It's been, I've been so lucky.
这一路走来，我真的是太幸运了。

1454
01:08:57.390 --> 01:09:00.270
I, I can't maybe do a play at some point.
我，我或许以后某天会去演个话剧吧。

1455
01:09:00.270 --> 01:09:00.410
Yeah.
对。

1456
01:09:00.450 --> 01:09:01.290
Would you ever do theater?
你还会演舞台剧吗？

1457
01:09:01.430 --> 01:09:01.530
Yeah.
会。

1458
01:09:01.750 --> 01:09:01.990
Yeah.
对。

1459
01:09:02.150 --> 01:09:06.350
And, and I've, you know, I've been talking to a couple of theaters about maybe doing
而且，而且我，你知道的，我一直在跟几家剧院聊，看能不能演

1460
01:09:06.350 --> 01:09:06.770
something.
点什么。

1461
01:09:07.610 --> 01:09:08.010
Yeah.
对。

1462
01:09:08.210 --> 01:09:09.250
Maybe somewhere down the road.
也许以后某个时候吧。

1463
01:09:09.410 --> 01:09:12.930
I haven't done a play in, well, since Nancy and I got married.
我有段时间没演过话剧了，嗯，自我和南希结婚以来就没演过。

1464
01:09:13.310 --> 01:09:16.310
It's been 27 years since I've done a play.
我已经有二十七年没演过话剧了。

1465
01:09:16.310 --> 01:09:16.890
So.
所以嘛。

1466
01:09:17.250 --> 01:09:19.230
But you are a classically trained actor.
但你可是受过古典戏剧训练的演员。

1467
01:09:19.510 --> 01:09:20.450
Oh, yes.
哦，是的。

1468
01:09:20.810 --> 01:09:21.030
Yes.
是的。

1469
01:09:21.410 --> 01:09:23.730
You, you were, you were of all of us.
你，你以前，在我们所有人当中。

1470
01:09:23.850 --> 01:09:27.830
We always talk about how like there were a bunch of the people who were the theater nerds.
我们总是聊起，比如当时剧组里有一群人是那种戏剧书呆子。

1471
01:09:27.830 --> 01:09:33.230
And then there were the like comedy, sketch, comedy, improv nerds on our set.
然后还有那种喜剧、小品、喜剧、即兴表演的书呆子。

1472
01:09:33.330 --> 01:09:34.070
But you were both.
但你两样都是。

1473
01:09:34.270 --> 01:09:36.370
You studied theater and also studied improv.
你既学过戏剧，也学过即兴表演。

1474
01:09:36.370 --> 01:09:37.150
I was just a nerd.
我只是个单纯的书呆子。

1475
01:09:38.830 --> 01:09:41.590
You double nerded it is what I'm getting at.
我的意思是，你是双料书呆子。

1476
01:09:43.010 --> 01:09:44.470
You, you did both.
你，你两样都做了。

1477
01:09:44.470 --> 01:09:44.910
Yeah.
对。

1478
01:09:45.130 --> 01:09:48.930
I mean, I, it was, yeah, I, I would like to do, I, I'm with you.
我是说，我，这，对，我，我也想演，我，我和你一样。

1479
01:09:49.190 --> 01:09:51.230
I, I'd like to do some, maybe we should do something together.
我，我也想搞点，也许我们应该一起合作点什么。

1480
01:09:51.390 --> 01:09:51.950
Let's do it.
我们干吧。

1481
01:09:52.250 --> 01:09:53.210
Oh, let's do some Broadway.
哦，去演百老汇吧。

1482
01:09:53.490 --> 01:09:54.770
I would come and watch it.
我会去看的。

1483
01:09:54.950 --> 01:09:55.730
With your hat.
戴着你的帽子。

1484
01:09:57.990 --> 01:10:02.890
And finally, Steve, you just worked with Mr. John Krasinski on his movie If.
最后，史蒂夫，你刚刚和约翰·卡拉辛斯基先生合作了他的电影《神秘友友》。

1485
01:10:03.010 --> 01:10:04.710
How was it to team up with him again?
再次和他搭档感觉怎么样？

1486
01:10:04.970 --> 01:10:05.490
Really fun.
非常有趣。

1487
01:10:05.730 --> 01:10:06.490
Was that great?
很棒对吧？

1488
01:10:07.290 --> 01:10:09.890
Well, I'm supposed to contractually, I'm supposed to say.
嗯，按合同规定，我必须这么说。

1489
01:10:09.930 --> 01:10:10.170
That's right.
没错。

1490
01:10:10.370 --> 01:10:10.530
Yeah.
对。

1491
01:10:10.990 --> 01:10:11.150
Yeah.
对。

1492
01:10:11.290 --> 01:10:12.530
Do you need to get out the piece of paper?
你需要把那张纸拿出来吗？

1493
01:10:12.670 --> 01:10:13.910
Do you want to read directly from it?
你想直接照着念吗？

1494
01:10:14.950 --> 01:10:17.310
John Krasinski is the most wonderful.
约翰·卡拉辛斯基是最棒的。

1495
01:10:18.350 --> 01:10:19.830
He, it was great.
他，真的很棒。

1496
01:10:20.190 --> 01:10:20.490
Aw.
噢。

1497
01:10:20.570 --> 01:10:22.390
He's, and he was such a good director.
他，而且他是个非常优秀的导演。

1498
01:10:22.630 --> 01:10:30.390
I mean, obviously since The Office, boy, has he like really shown himself as a fine director.
我的意思是，显然自从《办公室》以来，天哪，他真的展现出自己是一位优秀的导演了。

1499
01:10:30.630 --> 01:10:35.610
But did you know Janusz Kaminski is his DP on this movie?
但你知道雅努什·卡明斯基是这部电影的摄影指导吗？

1500
01:10:35.870 --> 01:10:36.130
No.
不知道。

1501
01:10:36.230 --> 01:10:37.950
Who is Steven Spielberg's DP.
谁是史蒂芬·斯皮尔伯格的摄影指导。

1502
01:10:37.950 --> 01:10:42.370
Like he is the best director of photography in the business.
就像他是业内最棒的摄影指导一样。

1503
01:10:42.550 --> 01:10:43.310
He's a legend.
他是个传奇。

1504
01:10:43.790 --> 01:10:45.590
And so, you know.
所以，你知道的。

1505
01:10:45.850 --> 01:10:46.310
Wow.
哇。

1506
01:10:46.550 --> 01:10:48.750
That's, it's a huge deal.
那是，这是一件大事。

1507
01:10:48.750 --> 01:10:51.470
And I think such a sign of respect to John.
而且我认为这是对约翰的一种尊重。

1508
01:10:51.850 --> 01:10:52.190
Right.
对的。

1509
01:10:52.190 --> 01:10:57.590
Like this person wants to, you know, wanted to work together with him.
就像这个人想要，你知道的，想要跟他合作。

1510
01:10:57.810 --> 01:11:00.810
So, that's, I, yeah.
所以，那是，我，是的。

1511
01:11:01.150 --> 01:11:04.130
He's, he's a, he's an amazing.
他，他是一个，他是一个了不起的人。

1512
01:11:04.330 --> 01:11:04.810
He's a big deal.
他是个大人物。

1513
01:11:04.990 --> 01:11:06.030
Amazingly talented guy.
才华横溢的家伙。

1514
01:11:06.750 --> 01:11:08.550
And so, yeah, just great to see him.
所以，是的，见到他太棒了。

1515
01:11:08.650 --> 01:11:09.170
Like you guys.
就像你们一样。

1516
01:11:09.330 --> 01:11:09.990
It's like, wow.
感觉就像，哇。

1517
01:11:10.510 --> 01:11:10.870
Yeah.
是的。

1518
01:11:11.030 --> 01:11:13.570
It's exactly like the last time we saw each other.
这跟我们上次见面时一模一样。

1519
01:11:13.710 --> 01:11:15.150
There's like no time has passed.
感觉就像时间没有流逝过一样。

1520
01:11:15.150 --> 01:11:17.150
We definitely felt that too.
我们绝对也有这种感觉。

1521
01:11:17.290 --> 01:11:19.870
Like when he zoomed in, we were just cracking up.
就像他放大画面时，我们都笑得前俯后仰。

1522
01:11:20.010 --> 01:11:23.570
We had to like stop laughing so we could do like our interview with him.
我们不得不停止笑声，以便能跟他进行采访。

1523
01:11:23.670 --> 01:11:24.870
Cause we just got so tickled.
因为我们实在太开心了。

1524
01:11:25.350 --> 01:11:26.210
I love that.
我太喜欢这样了。

1525
01:11:26.350 --> 01:11:30.850
This is, you know, BJ was on and he said to us, he was like, you guys, office family forever.
这是，你知道的，BJ上节目时对我们说，他就像，你们，办公室大家庭永远在一起。

1526
01:11:31.090 --> 01:11:32.970
And that's absolutely how I feel.
这绝对也是我的感受。

1527
01:11:33.350 --> 01:11:34.670
Like family.
就像家人一样。

1528
01:11:34.950 --> 01:11:36.190
Thanks for coming, Steve.
谢谢你能来，史蒂夫。

1529
01:11:36.530 --> 01:11:36.750
Yeah.
好的。

1530
01:11:37.070 --> 01:11:37.330
Whatever.
随便吧。

1531
01:11:39.350 --> 01:11:40.030
Oh, sorry.
哦，抱歉。

1532
01:11:40.110 --> 01:11:41.730
You got to get back to your leaf mulching.
你得回去弄你的碎树叶了。

1533
01:11:42.790 --> 01:11:43.230
Jeez.
